  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening quality infrastructure for sustainable rural value chains</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">St&#xe4;rkung der Qualit&#xe4;tsinfrastruktur f&#xfc;r nachhaltige l&#xe4;ndliche Wertsch&#xf6;pfungsketten</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Das Projekt tr&#xe4;gt zu einer st&#xe4;rkeren regionalen Integration der ECOWAS-Mitgliedsstaaten im Bereich der Metrologie bei. Die weniger fortgeschrittenen nationalen Metrologie-Institutionen in der Region werden in ihrer Leistungserbringung gest&#xe4;rkt sein und so ebenfalls aktiver am regionalen Austausch innerhalb ECOMET teilnehmen. Parallel dazu werden das ECOWAS Community Committee for Metrology (ECOMET) und seine Technischen Komitees weiterhin organisatorisch und strategisch gest&#xe4;rkt sein. Dies f&#xf6;rdert die Ownership der noch sehr jungen Struktur. Schlussendlich werden die weiter fortgeschrittenen nationalen Metrologie-Institutionen ihre Dienstleistungsorientierung und Sichtbarkeit beim Privatsektor verbessert haben, unter anderem entlang ausgew&#xe4;hlter Wertsch&#xf6;pfungsketten.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecuador ranks among the most biodiverse countries in the world. Its valorisation is an important element for the government to plan for a more diverse economy. A functioning quality infrastructure (QI) may contribute to ensuring the quality of non-traditional value chains in cultivation, processing, and transportation to target markets. Furthermore, quality assurance services support the design of (non-)traditional value chains towards a more sustainable production based on the application and verification of internationally recognised standards, for example in deforestation-free supply chains. In Ecuador, however, QI institutions have so far been insufficiently empowered to offer adequate services.
Key activities to achieve the project goals are divided into three pillars of action: (1) Strengthening the management competencies of partner institutions to further develop and position QI within Ecuador, (2) Promoting cooperation between QI institutions and sector actors in the field of agriculture, (3) Strengthening technical competencies in QI institutions for the development of relevant services.
Our project partners are the QI institutions in Ecuador: the national standards body (INEN) and the national accreditation service (SAE), the political counterpart is the Ministry of Production (MPCEIP). In addition, cooperation takes place with the relevant sector actors, such as the Ministry of Agriculture (MAG) and the Ministry of the Environment (MAATE) as well as conformity assessment bodies.
The project is implemented in close cooperation with projects of the German Agency for International Cooperation (GIZ) in the field of environmental protection and natural resources.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Die Akteure der Qualit&#xe4;tsinfrastruktur in Ecuador tragen zur Qualit&#xe4;t und &#xf6;kologischen Nachhaltigkeit in der Agrar- und Nahrungsmittelproduktion bei.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The quality infrastructure actors in Ecuador contribute to quality and environmental sustainability in the agricultural and food production.</narrative>
  </description>
